---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import Heading from "../components/Heading.astro"
import PostBody from "../components/PostBody.astro"
import SponsorCTA from "../components/SponsorCTA.astro"
import {
  getRepoDetails,
  getContributors,
  getSponsors,
  getReleases,
} from "../lib/api"
import { getActiveUsers } from "../lib/amplitude"
import { GITHUB_REPO } from "../const"

const title = `About DDEV`
const repoData = await getRepoDetails(GITHUB_REPO)
const contributorData = await getContributors(true)
const sponsorData = await getSponsors()
const releaseData = await getReleases()

const activeUsers = await getActiveUsers()

const count = (value: number | string) =>
  parseInt(String(value)).toLocaleString("en-US")

const stats = [
  { value: `${activeUsers.toLocaleString("en-US")}+`, label: "active users" },
  { value: count(releaseData.length), label: "releases" },
  { value: count(contributorData.length), label: "contributors" },
  { value: count(sponsorData.length), label: "sponsors" },
  { value: count(repoData.stargazers_count || 0), label: "GitHub stars" },
]
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={`A brief look at DDEV’s backstory and contributors.`}
>
  <main class="site-container mb-24">
    <Heading title={`The Story of DDEV`} />
    <div class="page-grid">
      <div class="site-gutter content-column">
        <PostBody>
          <p>
            DDEV is a local development environment for web developers. It
            originated within the company “Drud” in about 2016. Drud was
            building a general-purpose CLI for its infant web hosting product
            (named “DDEV-Live”, with the local dev tool named “DDEV-Local”), and
            was visionary enough to build local development into the idea.
            (Nobody really remembers what “DDEV” stands for, it might be “Docker
            development” or it might have been “Drud development”.)
          </p>

          <p>
            The independent value of the tool was soon recognized and it was
            refactored into its own repository, and then made open-source and it
            began its journey. Randy Fay was an employee of Drud in this period,
            and as a long-time proponent of local development and debugging was
            sold on its value. Drud graciously sponsored Randy to work on DDEV
            for nearly five years, until it lost its funding. DDEV of course had
            integration to Drud’s hosting product during this period, and it was
            seen as a way to bring developers into the Drud-hosting world.
          </p>

          <p>
            The company Drud (by then renamed “DDEV”) shut down in 2021 when it
            lost its venture funding. Randy Fay continued to maintain the
            project without interruption.
          </p>

          <p>
            In 2022, <a href="/blog/platform-sh-becomes-a-lead-sponsor-of-ddev/">Platform.sh
            stepped in as a major sponsor of DDEV</a>, continuing through its
            transition to the <a href="https://upsun.com">Upsun brand</a>, although at a lower level.
          </p>
          <p>
            In 2023, <a href="/blog/introducing-maintainer-stas">Stas Zhuk</a> came aboard as an additional maintainer, full-time since 2024, and has made
            amazing and constant contributions to the project.
          </p>
          <p>
            DDEV is an open-source project, free to all, and now has community governance via
            the <a href="/foundation">DDEV Foundation</a> and its Board of Directors.
          </p>

          <SponsorCTA />
        </PostBody>
      </div>
      <aside class="site-gutter sidebar-column">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-8">
          <div class="sidebar-card">
            <span
              class="sidebar-label"
            >
              DDEV Today
            </span>
            <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 lg:block dark:text-white">
              {
                stats.map((stat) => (
                  <li class="mt-4 first:mt-0">
                    <span class="text-4xl font-thin">{stat.value}</span>
                    <span class="block font-mono text-sm">{stat.label}</span>
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
